    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Audit coverage — measured, with denominators",
      "prov:value": "## The failure this exists to prevent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The failure this exists to prevent",
      "prov:value": "2026-09-23. An agent counted `kg-qa` sidecars over the bean store, found **zero**,\nand reported beans **\"effectively unaudited\"** — to the owner, as the premise for\nchoosing what to build next. **Eight gates audit them**: the five `check:bean-*`,\nplus `check:ready-to-close`, `check:stale-paths` and `check:harness-dirs`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The gate half is DECLARED, never inferred",
      "prov:value": "The tempting alternative is to infer it: grep each gate's source for a kind's\nname or its declared directory. **It fails in both directions at once.** A gate\nthat mentions `beans/defs/` in passing scores as auditing beans; a gate that\nresolves its directory through `directoriesForGraph` names no path and scores as\nauditing nothing. Both answers wrong, neither *looking* wrong — which is\n[`directory-conventions`](directory-conventions.md)' `dh4f`:\ncould-not-determine rendered as clean."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Five states, because three real gates cannot use a static list",
      "prov:value": "**That gap is closed as of bean `3srh`** — all 145 gates declare, so\n`audit:coverage:require-all` is wired in CI and the findings are verdicts rather\nthan bounds. The flag is what keeps it closed: a new gate arriving undeclared\nturns them back into an upper bound, silently, unless something fails. The\noutput still states the caveat whenever the count is non-zero, because the day\nit reopens is the day a reader needs to be told.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 3srh"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "When you cannot tell, do not annotate — and then go and read it",
      "prov:value": "Eleven gates were left undeclared on purpose at first, because each one's\ndocblock did not settle which declared kind its subject is, and **a fabricated\n`@covers` credits a kind with coverage nobody checked.** Under-claiming is\nrecoverable — the count says so out loud. Over-claiming looks like coverage."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "When you cannot tell, do not annotate — and then go and read it",
      "prov:value": "**The finding did not move** when the eleven were declared — the same four kinds,\nnow a verdict rather than a bound. That is what closing a denominator is for."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Four states per kind, and a single zero cannot tell them apart",
      "prov:value": "| state | what it means | the case that earns the name |\n|---|---|---|\n| `no-directory` | no instance declares one of this kind | `bean-defs`, declared inside `beans/beans.json`, reached through its parent — and carrying 8 gates |\n| `empty` | a directory exists and holds nothing | a determined empty |\n| `typed-only` | a declared validator TYPES its nodes; nothing judges them | none here, since bean `h1wq` |\n| `unaudited` | files, and nothing at all — not even a validator | none here, since bean `3oqj` |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean h1wq",
        "bean 3oqj"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "`typed-only` is a finding, and that is the whole reason it exists",
      "prov:value": "Bean `3oqj`. Before this state, `health` and `todos` read `unaudited` — and that\n**over-reported**. Both declare a validator, and `check:kind-validators` parses\ntheir nodes against it; they looked unreached only because the gate that types\nthem declares `@covers computed`, which this report counts as neither coverage\nnor gap.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 3oqj"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "`typed-only` is a finding, and that is the whole reason it exists",
      "prov:value": "**And it got closed.** The owner asked for all four to be judged (bean `h1wq`),\nso `check:harness-state` now carries one family per kind and `--strict` is green\nand wired in CI. The state stays, because the next kind to arrive will pass\nthrough it — and the flag is what stops it resting there.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean h1wq"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`typed-only` is a finding, and that is the whole reason it exists",
      "prov:value": "### The two kinds that were genuinely untyped"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Store the RELATION, print the census",
      "prov:value": "(The record was committed when this rule was written; it is now stored on the\n`qa-reports` branch keyed by commit. The rule is about what goes in it, and is\nunchanged.)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Store the RELATION, print the census",
      "prov:value": "The first version recorded `files` and `sidecars`. Two costs, and the second is\nthe one that kills a gate:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "What `--check` fails on, and what it does not",
      "prov:value": "`--check` **computes and judges, and writes nothing**. It fails on a finding\nthat is **NEW** against a baseline — a kind that lost its audit, a gate that\nstopped declaring, in the commit under review — and not on its own sidecar\nbeing stale. Staleness stopped being a question when derived QA results moved\nto the `qa-reports` branch (arc `3fva`, bean `0dav`): nothing committed is\nleft to be stale. The baseline is the committed working copy until bean\n`5hox` removes it, and `--against <ref>` (a `qa-reports` ref such as `main`)\nafter. **A baseline that is not there is UNKNOWN** — printed, never a pass,\nnever a failure, because an unwritten baseline is not this change's defect.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 0dav",
        "bean 3fva"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What `--check` fails on, and what it does not",
      "prov:value": "It used to fail on a stale sidecar, and the falsification pass caught that\nfirst version repairing the staleness it reported: red once, green on the\nrerun, the file still stale in the repository. The lesson survives the move:\n**a checker that mutates its own subject cannot be falsified**, which is the one\nproperty [`generalise-the-fix`](../../../sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/generalise-the-fix.md)\nMove 3 asks a guard to have."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What `--check` fails on, and what it does not",
      "prov:value": "**A kind whose directory is declared but absent from the checkout reads\n`unknown`, not `empty`** (the readers-audit's C8). With `test/results/` moved\naside, `qa` and `health` read `empty, 0` before this state existed — an absent\nanswer printed as a determined zero. A directory that declares `storage` reads\n`stored` instead: its files are on the branch, fetch them with `bun run\nqa:fetch`."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Adding a kind, or a gate",
      "prov:value": "- **A new gate**: add `@covers` in the same change. If you cannot tell which kind\n  its subject is, leave it off — the count is the honest answer.\n- **A new graph typology**: it appears in the report the moment it is registered,\n  because the denominator is the registry. Expect it to read `unaudited` until it\n  declares a validator and `typed-only` until something judges it — and say in\n  the sidecar why it needs nothing if that is the answer, never by letting the\n  row read clean.\n- **A relocation**: nothing to update. Directories resolve through\n  `directoriesForGraph`, which is the reason the report survived three layout\n  changes that broke prose in `AGENTS.md`."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Provenance",
      "prov:value": "Bean `folio-assistant-xutg`, written 2026-09-24 after the failure at the top of\nthis file. Split out of\n[`covered-is-not-reachable`](../../tools/folio-core/covered-is-not-reachable.md) the same day: added\nthere as a fifth case, it took that skill to 321 lines against a corpus p75 of\n279 and turned its own `skill-is-brief` criterion from a pass into a fail. That\nskill's footer already says what to do — *\"the remedy for a skill that has grown\na second subject is to split it, not to quiet the finding\"* — and the subject\nhere is different: a **kind of node**, not a mechanism.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean folio-assistant-xutg",
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
